"Deploy trpg through cryo-warden. REPO SIDE DONE (2026-08-13): .cryo-warden.json manifest (validated via aj cw validate-manifest) with three processes -- spacetimedb (a SEPARATE prod instance: spacetime start on TRPG_STDB_PORT with TRPG_STDB_DATA_DIR, per user decision), publisher (scripts/prod-publish.sh: waits for the instance, publishes WITHOUT --delete-data so prod data persists, tolerant bootstrap_admin with TRPG_ADMIN_TOKEN, then holds), web (vite preview of the built client on TRPG_WEB_PORT); build_command builds the client with VITE_STDB_PORT baked so browsers connect to the prod port (client change landed); required env: TRPG_STDB_PORT, TRPG_WEB_PORT, TRPG_STDB_DATA_DIR, TRPG_ADMIN_TOKEN, CARGO_TARGET_DIR (module compiles during generate/publish; keep cargo churn out of the immutable target dir). OPERATOR SIDE REMAINING (aj cw is the restricted gateway; registration/deploy need direct access): bare clone under CRYO_WARDEN_SOURCES_ROOT, POST /api/services, set the five env values, deploy master. ASSUMPTIONS TO VERIFY ON FIRST DEPLOY: spacetime start flag names (--listen-addr/--data-dir), spacetime+cargo+bun on cw's spawn PATH, cw proxy passing WebSockets (the stdb port carries ws), and the publisher hold pattern (sleep infinity) reading as healthy in cw. NOTE: no health_check declared ON PURPOSE -- spawn-first would double-open the persistent data dir."